# A copy of a spell is not cast (CR 707.10), so a copy of Faerie Fencing never "controlled a Faerie as you cast this spell": the
# ruling on the Dragon spells' same condition, "the copy wasn't cast, so whether you controlled a Dragon won't matter". The copy
# does copy X (CR 707.10). Bot1 controls Faerie Mastermind as it casts Fencing with X = 1 at Bot2's Rot-Curse Rakshasa (5/5), then
# flashes in Lutri, the Spellchaser, whose enters trigger copies Fencing, the copy aimed at Bot2's Concealing Curtains (0/4). The
# copy resolves first: -1/-1 and no bonus, so the Curtains are -1/3 (with the bonus they would die); then the original: -1/-1
# and -3/-3, so the Rakshasa is 1/1.

